Design an operational amplifier for task 10014.
The source row name (Sau_CFCC) is retained only for traceability; the design does not need to use that topology.
- Load capacitance (CLoad): 500 pF.
- The DC gain (dB) should be at least 90.
- The phase margin (degrees) should be at least 45.
- The phase margin (degrees) should be no more than 90.
- The power-supply rejection ratio, PSRR (dB) should be at least 60.
- The DC common-mode rejection ratio, CMRR (dB) should be at least 60.
- The absolute input-referred offset, |VOS| (V) should be no more than 0.0001.
- The absolute temperature coefficient, |TC| (1/°C) should be no more than 5e-05.
- The settling time (s) should be greater than 0.
- The settling time (s) should be no more than 5e-06.
- The power consumption (μW) should be greater than 0.
- The FOML = SR[V/μs] × CLoad[pF] / Power[mW] should be at least 1000.
- The FOMS = GBW[MHz] × CLoad[pF] / Power[mW] should be at least 5000.
